WEBVTT

00:00:03.670 --> 00:00:07.470
Captain's Log, Stardate 44614.6.

00:00:07.507 --> 00:00:10.374
We are approaching Starbase 313
where we will pick up

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:12.310
a shipment
of scientific equipment

00:00:12.345 --> 00:00:15.974
for transport to a Federation
outpost in the Guernica system.

00:00:16.016 --> 00:00:18.678
During the journey, we will
be hosting a special guest.

00:00:19.719 --> 00:00:21.983
Come.

00:00:22.088 --> 00:00:24.818
You wanted to see me, Captain?

00:00:24.858 --> 00:00:26.348
Yes, Mr. La Forge.

00:00:26.393 --> 00:00:29.453
It seems that the exemplary
nature of your work

00:00:29.496 --> 00:00:32.488
has caught the attention
of Starfleet Command.

00:00:32.532 --> 00:00:36.161
In fact, someone is coming
on board just to see

00:00:36.202 --> 00:00:38.670
the engine modifications
you've made.

00:00:38.705 --> 00:00:40.229
Who, Captain?

00:00:40.273 --> 00:00:41.740
The Senior Design Engineer

00:00:41.775 --> 00:00:44.835
at the Theoretical Propulsion
Group, Dr. Leah Brahms.

00:00:44.878 --> 00:00:48.541
Leah is coming here?

00:00:52.752 --> 00:00:54.379
Well, this is terrific.

00:00:54.421 --> 00:00:56.252
It is?

00:00:56.289 --> 00:00:58.280
Well, I mean, I've...

00:00:58.324 --> 00:01:01.885
studied her... schematics
for years.

00:01:01.928 --> 00:01:03.896
She was responsible for a lot

00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:06.194
of the engine design
on the Enterprise.

00:01:06.232 --> 00:01:08.496
Well, it should be
a very enjoyable visit then.

00:01:08.535 --> 00:01:09.968
She'll be transporting on board

00:01:10.070 --> 00:01:11.662
as soon as we reach
the starbase.

00:01:11.704 --> 00:01:14.935
Would you like to greet
her on our behalf?

00:01:14.974 --> 00:01:16.965
I would love to, Captain.

00:01:17.010 --> 00:01:18.534
Thank you.

00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:36.185
You keep picking at that uniform

00:01:36.229 --> 00:01:38.026
you're going to wear it out.

00:01:39.065 --> 00:01:41.397
I guess I am a little nervous.

00:01:41.434 --> 00:01:42.924
It's, uh... it's not every day

00:01:42.969 --> 00:01:44.994
a man comes face-to-face
with his dream.

00:01:45.105 --> 00:01:46.333
What?

00:01:46.372 --> 00:01:48.465
Okay, you remember
about a year ago

00:01:48.508 --> 00:01:50.840
when we were caught
in that booby trap

00:01:50.877 --> 00:01:52.242
the Menthars set?

00:01:52.278 --> 00:01:53.336
Mm-hmm.

00:01:53.379 --> 00:01:55.176
Okay. While we were trying
to get out of it

00:01:55.215 --> 00:01:57.615
I went down to the holodeck
to study an engine prototype

00:01:57.650 --> 00:01:59.948
that was made when the
Enterprise was first designed.

00:01:59.986 --> 00:02:04.218
And the computer... well, it
gave me an image of the engine

00:02:04.257 --> 00:02:07.749
but it also created
this hologram of the designer

00:02:07.794 --> 00:02:09.455
Dr. Leah Brahms.

00:02:09.496 --> 00:02:14.160
So, you met
a computer-simulated female?

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:18.933
Yeah, but not an ordinary
computer-simulated female.

00:02:18.972 --> 00:02:21.964
I mean, she was brilliant,
of course, but...

00:02:22.075 --> 00:02:24.202
warm, you know... friendly

00:02:24.244 --> 00:02:28.908
and it was like we worked
as one.

00:02:28.948 --> 00:02:31.314
I would start a sentence,
she'd finish it.

00:02:31.351 --> 00:02:32.909
What I didn't think of, she did.

00:02:32.952 --> 00:02:37.355
It was just... so comfortable.

00:02:37.390 --> 00:02:38.516
Hmm.

00:02:38.558 --> 00:02:41.083
Okay, I know it was
just a holographic image

00:02:41.127 --> 00:02:43.459
but the computer was able
to incorporate

00:02:43.496 --> 00:02:46.124
personality traits
from her Starfleet record.

00:02:46.166 --> 00:02:48.657
You know, Geordi,
everybody falls in love

00:02:48.701 --> 00:02:50.999
with a fantasy
every now and then.

00:02:51.037 --> 00:02:54.006
No, no, Guinan, see,
you've got it all wrong.

00:02:54.040 --> 00:02:57.737
I'm not necessarily expecting
anything romantic here.

00:02:57.777 --> 00:03:00.007
It's just, I know, whatever...

00:03:00.046 --> 00:03:03.812
Leah Brahms and I are going
to be good friends.

00:03:09.989 --> 00:03:12.719
Dr. Brahms is ready
to transport, sir.

00:03:12.759 --> 00:03:15.057
Okay, bring her over.

00:03:25.371 --> 00:03:26.770
Hi.

00:03:26.806 --> 00:03:27.966
I mean, uh...

00:03:28.074 --> 00:03:30.201
Welcome aboard, Dr. Brahms.

00:03:30.243 --> 00:03:33.701
I'm Lieutenant Commander
Geordi La Forge

00:03:33.746 --> 00:03:35.475
Chief Engineer.

00:03:35.515 --> 00:03:36.982
La Forge.

00:03:37.016 --> 00:03:41.350
So, you're the one who's
fouled up my engine designs.

00:04:12.619 --> 00:04:16.953
Space, the final frontier.

00:04:17.056 --> 00:04:20.890
These are the voyages
of the Starship Enterprise.

00:04:20.927 --> 00:04:22.895
Its continuing mission...

00:04:22.929 --> 00:04:26.865
to explore strange new worlds

00:04:26.899 --> 00:04:31.336
to seek out new life
and new civilizations

00:04:31.371 --> 00:04:35.865
to boldly go
where no one has gone before.

00:05:37.704 --> 00:05:40.764
The matter/anti-matter ratio
has been changed.

00:05:40.807 --> 00:05:43.640
The mixture isn't as rich
as regulations dictate.

00:05:43.676 --> 00:05:44.836
Experience has shown me

00:05:44.877 --> 00:05:46.469
that too high a ratio
diminishes efficiency.

00:05:46.512 --> 00:05:49.845
I worked with the mixture
until I found the right balance.

00:05:49.882 --> 00:05:52.680
The magnetic plasma transfer
to the warp field generators

00:05:52.719 --> 00:05:54.914
doesn't correspond
to the recommended specs.

00:05:54.954 --> 00:05:55.978
Right.

00:05:56.022 --> 00:05:57.614
Again, I adjusted the flow.

00:05:57.657 --> 00:05:59.989
Sometimes things happen
a little differently in space

00:06:00.059 --> 00:06:01.549
than they do
on the drawing board.

00:06:01.594 --> 00:06:03.027
Is that a criticism, Commander?

00:06:03.062 --> 00:06:04.495
No, of course not.

00:06:04.530 --> 00:06:06.430
It's just a well-known fact.

00:06:06.466 --> 00:06:08.263
There's theory
and there's application.

00:06:08.301 --> 00:06:09.893
They don't always jibe.

00:06:09.936 --> 00:06:12.063
You've charted a completely
new swap-out schedule

00:06:12.105 --> 00:06:13.470
for main components replacement.

00:06:13.506 --> 00:06:14.632
You bet.

00:06:14.674 --> 00:06:17.302
I found Starfleet estimates
for the MTBF units

00:06:17.343 --> 00:06:18.367
to be unrealistic.

00:06:18.411 --> 00:06:20.038
I simply determined
my own schedule

00:06:20.079 --> 00:06:23.242
based on observation
and experience.

00:06:23.282 --> 00:06:24.943
Is that going to be
your only defense, Commander?

00:06:24.984 --> 00:06:26.281
That same tired rhetoric?

00:06:26.319 --> 00:06:28.617
"Out here in the field,
we learn things

00:06:28.654 --> 00:06:31.054
you designers couldn't
possibly understand."

00:06:31.090 --> 00:06:33.320
In the first place, Doctor, I'm
not aware of needing any defense

00:06:33.359 --> 00:06:35.327
and, in the second place,
if you're determined to be...

00:06:35.361 --> 00:06:38.626
Dr. Brahms, you have
an incoming message on subspace.

00:06:38.664 --> 00:06:40.859
I'd like to hear
this message privately.

00:06:40.900 --> 00:06:42.162
In my office.

00:06:42.201 --> 00:06:43.259
Be my guest.

00:06:43.302 --> 00:06:44.496
Thank you.

00:06:48.808 --> 00:06:51.743
Commander, I am picking up
some unusual readings

00:06:51.778 --> 00:06:53.541
in the Alpha Omicron system.

00:06:53.579 --> 00:06:56.571
At this range,
all I am able to discern

00:06:56.616 --> 00:06:59.449
is that it is
an asymmetrical field

00:06:59.485 --> 00:07:00.611
of intense energy.

00:07:00.653 --> 00:07:03.053
What type
of radiation signature?

00:07:03.089 --> 00:07:05.114
Unknown, sir.

00:07:05.158 --> 00:07:08.491
The Alpha Omicron system
has yet to be charted.

00:07:08.528 --> 00:07:10.428
I recommend
we take this opportunity

00:07:10.463 --> 00:07:11.623
for further research.

00:07:11.664 --> 00:07:14.929
Well, we're
way ahead of schedule.

00:07:15.034 --> 00:07:19.562
Alter course for Alpha Omicron.

00:07:28.147 --> 00:07:31.639
Dr. Brahms, there's no reason
for us to argue.

00:07:31.684 --> 00:07:33.447
We're on the same side here.

00:07:33.486 --> 00:07:35.215
I'm aware of that.

00:07:35.254 --> 00:07:38.314
So, why don't I take you
on a little tour.

00:07:38.357 --> 00:07:40.086
Show you the adjustments
I've made

00:07:40.126 --> 00:07:41.218
why I think they work

00:07:41.260 --> 00:07:44.627
and we can begin pulling
together on this?

00:07:44.664 --> 00:07:46.359
Okay.

00:07:46.399 --> 00:07:49.664
And why not start
with the dilithium chamber.

00:07:53.005 --> 00:07:54.632
Okay?

00:07:54.674 --> 00:07:56.699
Okay.

00:07:56.742 --> 00:07:59.802
The anomaly is orbiting
the seventh planet, sir.

00:07:59.846 --> 00:08:02.076
It is a mass of plasma energy

00:08:02.114 --> 00:08:04.014
contained
within discrete boundaries

00:08:04.050 --> 00:08:06.678
by an outer covering
of silicates, actinides

00:08:06.719 --> 00:08:09.017
and carbonaceous chondrites.

00:08:09.055 --> 00:08:11.546
On screen.

00:08:11.591 --> 00:08:13.718
Magnify.

00:08:15.628 --> 00:08:17.823
Is it a ship?

00:08:17.864 --> 00:08:19.855
It does not conform
to any known design.

00:08:19.899 --> 00:08:22.424
Any records of similar phenomena
in Starfleet listings?

00:08:22.468 --> 00:08:23.435
No, sir.

00:08:23.469 --> 00:08:25.528
This has never been seen before.

00:08:29.408 --> 00:08:31.603
Ensign Rager,
ahead one quarter impulse.

00:08:31.644 --> 00:08:32.770
Aye, sir.

00:08:32.812 --> 00:08:35.280
Put us in orbit
of the seventh planet.

00:08:35.314 --> 00:08:36.872
Keep us a relative distance

00:08:36.916 --> 00:08:38.941
of ten kilometers
from the object.

00:08:38.985 --> 00:08:40.680
Alert science stations
to stand by.

00:08:40.720 --> 00:08:42.779
Tell them to coordinate
all efforts with Commander Data.

00:08:42.822 --> 00:08:43.948
Aye, sir.

00:08:47.660 --> 00:08:49.355
What happened here?

00:08:49.395 --> 00:08:50.692
Who did this?

00:08:50.730 --> 00:08:52.698
You remember, the crystal's
been reoriented

00:08:52.732 --> 00:08:54.427
to adjust the direction

00:08:54.467 --> 00:08:56.128
of the lattice structure.

00:08:56.168 --> 00:08:57.635
Remember?
Why would I remember?

00:08:57.670 --> 00:08:59.570
Right, why would you?

00:08:59.605 --> 00:09:02.904
Uh... well, the ship was
experiencing some difficulty

00:09:03.009 --> 00:09:04.738
and we made this adjustment

00:09:04.777 --> 00:09:08.235
hoping that it would work
and it did.

00:09:08.281 --> 00:09:10.340
So, it was your idea?

00:09:10.383 --> 00:09:13.409
Not exclusively, no.

00:09:13.452 --> 00:09:14.749
It's curious.

00:09:14.787 --> 00:09:18.883
This modification
was due to be introduced...

00:09:18.925 --> 00:09:21.359
In the next class starship.

00:09:21.394 --> 00:09:22.622
Yes.

00:09:25.731 --> 00:09:27.892
How did you know that?

00:09:27.934 --> 00:09:30.266
Um... I didn't.

00:09:30.303 --> 00:09:32.362
I mean...

00:09:32.405 --> 00:09:35.533
Well, it's
the next logical step, right?

00:09:35.575 --> 00:09:37.202
Listen, Doctor.

00:09:37.243 --> 00:09:39.734
Sometimes we have to fly by
the seat of our pants out here.

00:09:39.779 --> 00:09:41.610
So it stands to reason
that once in a while

00:09:41.647 --> 00:09:44.013
we're going to come up
with the same solutions you do.

00:09:49.488 --> 00:09:52.252
Listen,
I've got a personnel review

00:09:52.291 --> 00:09:54.418
scheduled to start
in about five minutes

00:09:54.460 --> 00:09:56.553
and I know it's been
a long day for you.

00:09:56.596 --> 00:09:58.496
So, why don't we get
together later?

00:09:58.531 --> 00:10:01.295
Sort of plan out our agenda
for the next day or two.

00:10:01.334 --> 00:10:02.494
Agenda?

00:10:02.535 --> 00:10:04.332
What it is we want
to accomplish here.

00:10:04.370 --> 00:10:06.497
How we might best
go about that.

00:10:06.539 --> 00:10:09.633
Maybe even get to know
each other a little bit.

00:10:09.675 --> 00:10:12.906
It might make this easier.

00:10:12.945 --> 00:10:14.742
Maybe you're right.

00:10:14.780 --> 00:10:15.974
Okay, great.

00:10:16.082 --> 00:10:19.779
How about, uh... my quarters?

00:10:19.819 --> 00:10:22.219
1900 hours?

00:10:22.254 --> 00:10:24.154
Maybe even have a bite to eat?

00:10:24.190 --> 00:10:26.420
I make a great fungilli.

00:10:26.459 --> 00:10:29.189
I love fungilli.

00:10:29.228 --> 00:10:31.492
Is that right?

00:10:31.530 --> 00:10:33.054
Huh.

00:10:47.011 --> 00:10:50.811
Sensors are having difficulty
penetrating the interior.

00:10:50.849 --> 00:10:53.818
However, the radiated output
suggests a coherent system

00:10:53.852 --> 00:10:56.616
of energy storage
and utilization.

00:10:56.654 --> 00:10:59.316
Then it was constructed
by someone?

00:10:59.357 --> 00:11:00.619
It is a possibility.

00:11:00.658 --> 00:11:02.785
However, the sensor data
gathered thus far

00:11:02.827 --> 00:11:04.795
suggests a naturally
occurring phenomenon

00:11:04.829 --> 00:11:06.558
with biological properties.

00:11:06.598 --> 00:11:07.963
A life-form?

00:11:07.999 --> 00:11:09.432
Yes, Captain.

00:11:10.969 --> 00:11:14.530
Mr. Worf, begin compiling
readings for transmission

00:11:14.572 --> 00:11:16.062
to Starfleet Headquarters.

00:11:16.107 --> 00:11:19.133
Mr. Data, prepare to launch
three level-5 probes.

00:11:19.177 --> 00:11:20.906
Ensign, aft thrusters.

00:11:20.945 --> 00:11:23.413
Standard observational posture.

00:11:23.448 --> 00:11:26.975
Level-5 probe sequence
ready for launch, Commander.

00:11:27.018 --> 00:11:27.985
On your mark.

00:11:28.086 --> 00:11:29.713
Stand by, Mr. Data.

00:11:29.754 --> 00:11:30.743
Aye, sir.

00:11:33.691 --> 00:11:35.784
What would it be like,
Counselor?

00:11:35.827 --> 00:11:39.388
No ship, no bulky space suits.

00:11:39.430 --> 00:11:41.864
Just to live between the stars

00:11:41.900 --> 00:11:44.198
and have the entire galaxy
as a home.

00:11:48.873 --> 00:11:51.501
Captain, we are being probed.

00:11:51.542 --> 00:11:53.669
Recommend we raise shields.

00:11:53.711 --> 00:11:55.576
Negative, Mr. Worf.

00:11:55.613 --> 00:11:58.446
We are curious about it.

00:11:58.483 --> 00:12:01.452
It has a perfect right
to be curious about us.

00:12:03.321 --> 00:12:05.312
Change in readings, sir.

00:12:05.356 --> 00:12:08.348
The life-form has increased
its energy output by 50%.

00:12:08.393 --> 00:12:09.951
It is moving toward us.

00:12:10.061 --> 00:12:11.926
Reverse course, Ensign.

00:12:11.963 --> 00:12:13.624
300 kph.

00:12:13.665 --> 00:12:14.825
Aye, sir.

00:12:14.866 --> 00:12:16.231
Now, easy.

00:12:16.267 --> 00:12:18.667
We don't want to alarm
or provoke it.

00:12:31.449 --> 00:12:33.974
We are caught
in an energy damping field, sir.

00:12:34.018 --> 00:12:35.747
Raise shields.

00:12:37.388 --> 00:12:38.855
No effect, Captain.

00:12:38.890 --> 00:12:42.291
Reverse power, full impulse.

00:12:42.327 --> 00:12:44.386
Impulse engines at full power.

00:12:44.429 --> 00:12:47.227
No change in position, sir.

00:12:47.265 --> 00:12:48.596
Red Alert!

00:12:50.835 --> 00:12:54.100
Mr. La Forge,
prepare to initiate warp drive.

00:12:54.138 --> 00:12:55.264
Sorry, Captain.

00:12:55.306 --> 00:12:57.831
There's too much interference
to form a warp field.

00:12:57.875 --> 00:12:58.933
Warning.

00:12:58.977 --> 00:13:02.538
Radiation levels
at 65 millirads per minute

00:13:02.580 --> 00:13:03.547
and rising.

00:13:03.581 --> 00:13:04.946
Riker to Dr. Crusher.

00:13:04.983 --> 00:13:06.280
Go ahead, Commander.

00:13:06.317 --> 00:13:08.547
All decks prepare
for radiation protocol.

00:13:08.586 --> 00:13:09.780
Acknowledged. Crusher out.

00:13:09.821 --> 00:13:10.879
Warning.

00:13:10.922 --> 00:13:13.789
Radiation levels at 300
millirads per minute and rising.

00:13:13.825 --> 00:13:15.850
Lethal exposure in one minute.

00:13:15.893 --> 00:13:17.952
Mr. Worf, ready phasers.

00:13:18.029 --> 00:13:20.259
Minimum power.

00:13:20.298 --> 00:13:21.697
Ready.

00:13:24.402 --> 00:13:25.630
Fire.

00:13:32.176 --> 00:13:35.145
Radiation levels dropping back
to normal, Captain.

00:13:35.179 --> 00:13:38.637
Energy patterns are
breaking down, sir.

00:13:40.184 --> 00:13:44.518
The radiation signature
is no longer stable.

00:13:46.190 --> 00:13:48.021
Energy output is negligible,
sir.

00:13:50.395 --> 00:13:52.363
Radiation patterns...

00:13:52.397 --> 00:13:54.365
no longer coherent.

00:13:57.368 --> 00:13:59.336
I believe it is dead, sir.

00:14:16.154 --> 00:14:18.952
We're out here to explore

00:14:19.057 --> 00:14:21.787
to make contact
with other life-forms

00:14:21.826 --> 00:14:26.957
to establish peaceful relations,
but not to interfere...

00:14:26.998 --> 00:14:29.990
and absolutely not to destroy.

00:14:33.671 --> 00:14:37.971
And yet, look
at what we have just done.

00:14:38.076 --> 00:14:40.135
Captain, everything you did

00:14:40.178 --> 00:14:43.636
was consistent with established
Starfleet procedures.

00:14:46.284 --> 00:14:48.218
Number One, you have the Bridge.

00:14:51.355 --> 00:14:54.085
Captain, sensors are picking up

00:14:54.125 --> 00:14:57.686
a new energy reading
from the life-form.

00:14:57.728 --> 00:14:59.923
Elaborate, Data.

00:14:59.964 --> 00:15:03.422
There is a new concentration
of ionizing radiation

00:15:03.468 --> 00:15:07.268
growing in the center
of its body.

00:15:07.305 --> 00:15:08.795
Then...

00:15:13.311 --> 00:15:15.472
perhaps it's still alive.

00:15:18.816 --> 00:15:20.147
Okay.

00:15:21.319 --> 00:15:25.187
Computer, subdued lighting.

00:15:25.223 --> 00:15:27.282
No, that's... that's too much.

00:15:27.325 --> 00:15:29.452
I-I don't want it dark.

00:15:29.494 --> 00:15:31.621
I want it cozy.

00:15:31.662 --> 00:15:35.621
Please state your request
in precise candlepower.

00:15:35.666 --> 00:15:38.134
See, it's not a matter
of precision, computer.

00:15:38.169 --> 00:15:40.160
It's a matter of mood.

00:15:40.204 --> 00:15:43.196
Brighter than this.

00:15:43.241 --> 00:15:46.972
Hmm. More.

00:15:47.011 --> 00:15:50.139
More...

00:15:50.181 --> 00:15:52.809
A little more.

00:15:52.850 --> 00:15:54.613
Hold! Right there.

00:15:54.652 --> 00:15:55.983
Perfect.

00:15:56.020 --> 00:15:59.080
Now, some, um, some music.

00:15:59.123 --> 00:16:01.216
Maybe, uh...

00:16:01.259 --> 00:16:04.456
maybe a little soft jazz.

00:16:05.963 --> 00:16:07.931
Mm. No, that's...
that's not right.

00:16:07.965 --> 00:16:09.592
Let me think here.

00:16:09.634 --> 00:16:11.602
Oh, I got it.

00:16:11.636 --> 00:16:14.161
Uh, some Brahms.

00:16:14.205 --> 00:16:16.298
A piano étude.

00:16:18.809 --> 00:16:23.610
Mm... no, that's, uh...
that's too corny.

00:16:23.648 --> 00:16:24.615
Hmm.

00:16:24.649 --> 00:16:27.117
Probably everybody
thinks of that.

00:16:27.151 --> 00:16:29.449
Computer, just give me
some guitar.

00:16:29.487 --> 00:16:30.784
Classical guitar.

00:16:30.821 --> 00:16:32.482
Doesn't matter who.

00:16:34.158 --> 00:16:36.319
Yes. Thank you.

00:16:43.668 --> 00:16:46.159
Come on in.

00:16:46.204 --> 00:16:50.641
Oh, uh... you've changed.

00:16:50.675 --> 00:16:52.472
Yeah.

00:16:52.510 --> 00:16:55.968
Uniforms are so... formal.

00:16:56.080 --> 00:16:59.914
You're less formal than
any Starfleet officer

00:16:59.951 --> 00:17:02.078
I've ever met, Commander.

00:17:02.119 --> 00:17:03.746
Am I?

00:17:03.788 --> 00:17:07.246
I really just wanted to make you
feel more comfortable.

00:17:07.291 --> 00:17:09.282
I'm fine, thank you.

00:17:10.795 --> 00:17:12.262
I'm sorry.

00:17:12.296 --> 00:17:15.788
Come in and, uh, have a seat.

00:17:17.802 --> 00:17:19.429
Uh, can I get you a drink?

00:17:19.470 --> 00:17:20.596
No, thank you.

00:17:20.638 --> 00:17:21.605
You sure?

00:17:21.639 --> 00:17:23.266
Mm-hmm.

00:17:23.307 --> 00:17:25.275
You know...

00:17:25.309 --> 00:17:29.268
your hair... it's, uh...

00:17:29.313 --> 00:17:31.611
it's different.

00:17:31.649 --> 00:17:34.550
Different than a few hours ago?

00:17:34.585 --> 00:17:37.782
No, I mean it's different
than I expected.

00:17:37.822 --> 00:17:40.382
Different from
your Starfleet records.

00:17:40.424 --> 00:17:43.951
Oh, yes, I used to wear it up.

00:17:43.995 --> 00:17:44.962
Yeah.

00:17:45.062 --> 00:17:47.428
Why would you need to see
my personnel files?

00:17:49.333 --> 00:17:52.131
Standard procedure
when guests come on board...

00:17:52.169 --> 00:17:53.227
protocol.

00:17:53.271 --> 00:17:55.569
I mean, it was nothing specific
actually.

00:17:55.606 --> 00:17:57.904
Just, you know...

00:17:57.942 --> 00:18:00.809
Commander La Forge...

00:18:00.845 --> 00:18:06.249
if I seem to be somewhat
unyielding in my views

00:18:06.284 --> 00:18:10.687
it's because I care so very much
about my work.

00:18:10.721 --> 00:18:13.451
Oh, I-I know.

00:18:13.491 --> 00:18:18.053
To be honest,
people find me... cold

00:18:18.095 --> 00:18:22.623
cerebral, lacking in humor...

00:18:22.667 --> 00:18:24.601
But they're wrong.

00:18:24.635 --> 00:18:26.034
I assure you.

00:18:27.571 --> 00:18:30.369
Well, I try not to be that way

00:18:30.408 --> 00:18:35.912
but when it comes to my designs,
my engines, especially the ones

00:18:36.045 --> 00:18:37.137
on the Enterprise...

00:18:37.179 --> 00:18:40.273
It's like...

00:18:40.316 --> 00:18:42.079
they're your children.

00:18:42.118 --> 00:18:45.918
Yes. Exactly.

00:18:45.955 --> 00:18:49.482
So, naturally, you're
a little possessive about them.

00:18:49.525 --> 00:18:53.621
You understand that?

00:18:53.663 --> 00:18:54.891
Yes, I do.

00:18:54.931 --> 00:18:58.958
You see...
I feel the same way.

00:18:59.068 --> 00:19:01.559
That's amazing.

00:19:01.604 --> 00:19:04.698
I don't think anyone has ever...

00:19:07.109 --> 00:19:09.543
Sometimes I feel
more comfortable

00:19:09.578 --> 00:19:12.172
with engine schematics
than people.

00:19:12.214 --> 00:19:17.709
Well, maybe you just haven't
met the right... people.

00:19:21.590 --> 00:19:23.182
You hungry?

00:19:23.225 --> 00:19:24.749
I'm hungry.

00:19:24.794 --> 00:19:26.728
Why don't
I just start dinner, okay?

00:19:26.762 --> 00:19:28.696
Commander...

00:19:28.731 --> 00:19:31.199
Please, call me Geordi.

00:19:31.233 --> 00:19:32.598
I'm sorry.

00:19:32.635 --> 00:19:35.763
I hope that I didn't put you
to a lot of trouble

00:19:35.805 --> 00:19:37.136
but I can't stay.

00:19:37.173 --> 00:19:38.765
You can't?

00:19:38.808 --> 00:19:41.936
I just don't think
that it's appropriate.

00:19:41.978 --> 00:19:44.845
Oh, uh-huh.

00:19:44.880 --> 00:19:47.849
I'll meet with you
at 0800 tomorrow?

00:19:47.883 --> 00:19:50.351
I'm preparing
a list of discrepancies

00:19:50.386 --> 00:19:53.287
that I've identified
in your modifications.

00:19:53.322 --> 00:19:54.755
I hope...

00:19:54.790 --> 00:19:56.951
now that we've reached
an understanding...

00:19:56.993 --> 00:20:00.360
that you'll be prepared
to discuss them with me

00:20:00.396 --> 00:20:01.954
in a more objective fashion.

00:20:03.332 --> 00:20:05.459
Sure. Fine.

00:20:05.501 --> 00:20:06.798
Thank you.

00:20:06.836 --> 00:20:08.360
Good night, Commander.

00:20:14.010 --> 00:20:15.500
Good night.

00:20:17.513 --> 00:20:20.209
This new concentration
of energy was detected

00:20:20.249 --> 00:20:23.218
only after the surrounding
material became inert.

00:20:23.252 --> 00:20:25.982
Could this be some sort
of tissue regeneration?

00:20:26.088 --> 00:20:28.989
The radiation signature is
similar to the original pattern

00:20:29.025 --> 00:20:30.720
but with significant
differences.

00:20:30.760 --> 00:20:34.355
Some kind of reaction
to our phaser fire, perhaps?

00:20:34.397 --> 00:20:36.262
I believe it is separate
and self-contained

00:20:36.298 --> 00:20:37.959
within the body
of the dead life-form.

00:20:38.000 --> 00:20:39.331
Another entity.

00:20:39.368 --> 00:20:40.733
Yes, sir.

00:20:40.770 --> 00:20:42.465
It appears to be

00:20:42.505 --> 00:20:44.405
a smaller,
less-developed version

00:20:44.440 --> 00:20:46.237
of the original creature.

00:20:46.275 --> 00:20:47.242
Huh.

00:20:47.276 --> 00:20:49.938
No wonder it attacked us.

00:20:49.979 --> 00:20:53.540
It was about to give birth.

00:21:05.694 --> 00:21:07.127
Doctor.

00:21:07.163 --> 00:21:10.428
It's dangerous to generalize
about new life-forms

00:21:10.466 --> 00:21:12.696
but based on my experience
with other beings

00:21:12.735 --> 00:21:14.498
who bear their young
in this manner

00:21:14.537 --> 00:21:18.132
I'd say that the offspring
is still premature.

00:21:18.174 --> 00:21:20.267
Otherwise, it would be able
to break through

00:21:20.309 --> 00:21:21.970
the outer body shell
of the parent.

00:21:22.078 --> 00:21:23.340
Will this creature

00:21:23.379 --> 00:21:26.473
be able to survive on its own
without the parent?

00:21:26.515 --> 00:21:28.449
There's no way to tell.

00:21:28.484 --> 00:21:31.146
We don't have enough information
about the biofunctions

00:21:31.187 --> 00:21:33.781
of the adult,
much less the child.

00:21:33.823 --> 00:21:35.882
Is there anything
we can do to help?

00:21:35.925 --> 00:21:40.225
If we were in Sick Bay,
I'd try a cesarean section.

00:21:40.262 --> 00:21:41.786
The first priority

00:21:41.831 --> 00:21:44.163
is to free it
from the body of the parent.

00:21:44.200 --> 00:21:46.361
We could use our phasers
as a scalpel.

00:21:46.402 --> 00:21:48.199
Yes, that might work.

00:21:48.237 --> 00:21:50.000
I advise against this, Captain.

00:21:50.072 --> 00:21:52.802
The parent proved to be
a threat to the ship.

00:21:52.842 --> 00:21:56.334
We do not know
how the offspring will react.

00:21:56.378 --> 00:21:58.972
Your objection is noted,
Mr. Worf

00:21:59.014 --> 00:22:03.474
but we are directly responsible
for the death of the parent.

00:22:03.519 --> 00:22:06.955
We cannot simply wash our hands
of it now.

00:22:07.022 --> 00:22:09.013
Doctor, we will proceed
at your discretion.

00:22:15.531 --> 00:22:16.828
Good morning.

00:22:16.866 --> 00:22:18.163
Good morning.

00:22:18.200 --> 00:22:19.497
The first thing I'd like to do

00:22:19.535 --> 00:22:21.264
is inspect the power
transfer conduits.

00:22:21.303 --> 00:22:24.761
You realize the only way to
inspect them is to crawl inside.

00:22:24.807 --> 00:22:27.173
I designed them, Commander.

00:22:27.209 --> 00:22:29.370
I know what's involved.

00:22:36.218 --> 00:22:38.345
Here we go.

00:22:38.387 --> 00:22:40.548
Power taps... watch yourself.

00:22:43.392 --> 00:22:46.884
The acoustic signature
doesn't sound right.

00:22:46.929 --> 00:22:49.193
You're probably the only
other person in the galaxy

00:22:49.231 --> 00:22:50.789
who could pick that up.

00:22:50.833 --> 00:22:52.494
What's causing it?

00:22:52.535 --> 00:22:54.765
It's right up here.

00:22:54.803 --> 00:22:58.637
I've never seen anything
like this before.

00:22:58.674 --> 00:22:59.936
What is it?

00:22:59.975 --> 00:23:03.206
It's a mid-range phase adjuster.

00:23:03.245 --> 00:23:06.908
Puts the plasma back into phase
after inertial distortion.

00:23:06.949 --> 00:23:09.509
This has never been done before.

00:23:09.552 --> 00:23:10.541
I don't even think

00:23:10.586 --> 00:23:13.111
this has ever even been
conceived of before.

00:23:13.155 --> 00:23:15.521
You should write
a scientific paper.

00:23:16.859 --> 00:23:18.087
Uh-uh, Doctor, no.

00:23:18.127 --> 00:23:21.324
Writing is not
one of my strong suits.

00:23:21.363 --> 00:23:25.459
But this kind of refinement
should be shared

00:23:25.501 --> 00:23:27.492
and you deserve
the credit for it.

00:23:27.536 --> 00:23:31.165
Well, maybe we could, uh...
collaborate.

00:23:31.207 --> 00:23:34.176
Writing is one
of your strong points.

00:23:40.783 --> 00:23:42.478
Commander La Forge...

00:23:42.518 --> 00:23:45.316
ever since I came on board

00:23:45.354 --> 00:23:49.188
there seems to be something
a little peculiar

00:23:49.225 --> 00:23:51.955
about your attitude.

00:23:51.994 --> 00:23:54.963
You seem to know
things about me...

00:23:54.997 --> 00:23:57.488
even though we've never met.

00:24:01.003 --> 00:24:02.300
Well, uh...

00:24:04.340 --> 00:24:07.275
to tell you, uh,
to tell you the truth

00:24:08.277 --> 00:24:09.869
I've studied you.

00:24:09.912 --> 00:24:14.645
Your writings,
your Starfleet file.

00:24:14.683 --> 00:24:16.514
I've admired you.

00:24:16.552 --> 00:24:18.611
You know, your... your work.

00:24:18.654 --> 00:24:21.145
Well, I'm flattered, but...

00:24:21.190 --> 00:24:22.885
And...

00:24:25.327 --> 00:24:26.487
Ah...

00:24:26.528 --> 00:24:28.496
Well, I really...

00:24:28.530 --> 00:24:31.658
I really wanted to meet you
for a long time

00:24:31.700 --> 00:24:35.192
and... I'd like to think

00:24:35.237 --> 00:24:39.867
that... we could become friends.

00:24:39.908 --> 00:24:42.968
Maybe good friends.

00:24:43.012 --> 00:24:45.207
I thought you knew.

00:24:48.550 --> 00:24:51.610
I mean, you know
everything else about me.

00:24:51.654 --> 00:24:55.351
But, Commander, um...

00:24:55.391 --> 00:24:59.191
if I'm hearing
what I think I'm hearing

00:24:59.228 --> 00:25:02.356
then you should know

00:25:02.398 --> 00:25:05.196
that I'm married.

00:25:14.677 --> 00:25:18.135
Set phaser power
to three percent, narrow beam.

00:25:18.180 --> 00:25:19.807
Three percent.

00:25:19.848 --> 00:25:20.974
All right.

00:25:22.017 --> 00:25:24.076
Here we go.

00:25:29.625 --> 00:25:31.957
The first incision is complete.

00:25:32.061 --> 00:25:33.961
Ideally, the offspring
should now be able

00:25:33.996 --> 00:25:36.726
to push through the outer shell
of the parent by itself.

00:25:39.768 --> 00:25:42.134
I think it needs
a little more help.

00:25:42.171 --> 00:25:44.162
We've done all we can.

00:25:44.206 --> 00:25:48.575
I don't want to risk hitting
the offspring by accident.

00:25:52.114 --> 00:25:53.604
Come on.

00:25:53.649 --> 00:25:55.776
You can do it.

00:26:04.526 --> 00:26:06.687
Ah! Captain

00:26:06.729 --> 00:26:11.757
I'd like to announce the birth
of a large baby... something.

00:26:13.268 --> 00:26:15.065
Well done, Doctor.

00:26:17.139 --> 00:26:18.299
Well done.

00:26:21.143 --> 00:26:22.940
How could it have been
so far off?

00:26:23.045 --> 00:26:25.445
It was based on every
piece of information

00:26:25.480 --> 00:26:27.141
on record about Leah Brahms...

00:26:27.182 --> 00:26:30.208
okay, with an admitted
margin for error

00:26:30.252 --> 00:26:35.053
but this is an error that's
about a light-year wide.

00:26:35.090 --> 00:26:36.785
Not what you hoped for, huh?

00:26:36.825 --> 00:26:38.884
Hoped... Guinan

00:26:38.927 --> 00:26:43.387
the woman is about as friendly
as a Circassian Plague Cat.

00:26:43.432 --> 00:26:45.957
Only cares about her work

00:26:46.001 --> 00:26:49.630
hates what I've done
to her engines

00:26:49.671 --> 00:26:53.664
and, to top it all off,
she's married.

00:26:53.709 --> 00:26:57.167
The computer never even told me
she was married.

00:26:57.212 --> 00:26:58.679
Computer glitch?

00:26:58.714 --> 00:27:00.841
Must have been.

00:27:00.882 --> 00:27:04.045
Maybe it was your old VISOR.

00:27:04.086 --> 00:27:06.452
What are you talking about?

00:27:06.488 --> 00:27:09.480
Well, the one you wore when you
were on the holodeck with her.

00:27:09.524 --> 00:27:14.461
Guinan, it's the same VISOR.

00:27:14.496 --> 00:27:16.896
Really?

00:27:16.932 --> 00:27:18.923
Oh, I figured it was
probably the one

00:27:18.967 --> 00:27:21.128
that lets you see
what you want to see.

00:27:22.704 --> 00:27:24.695
What's that supposed to mean?

00:27:24.740 --> 00:27:29.040
You saw exactly what you wanted
to see on the holodeck.

00:27:29.077 --> 00:27:31.705
Sure, the computer made it
look like her

00:27:31.747 --> 00:27:33.612
gave it personality

00:27:33.648 --> 00:27:36.276
but when it came
to the relationship, La Forge

00:27:36.318 --> 00:27:37.945
you... filled in the blanks.

00:27:37.986 --> 00:27:40.784
And you had
a perfectly wonderful

00:27:40.822 --> 00:27:42.949
marvelous little fantasy

00:27:42.991 --> 00:27:46.586
until the real Leah showed up
and ruined it.

00:27:46.628 --> 00:27:49.722
Now, she's probably done
the most horrific thing

00:27:49.765 --> 00:27:51.790
one person can do to another...

00:27:51.833 --> 00:27:54.927
not live up
to your expectations.

00:27:54.970 --> 00:28:00.602
So I'd take a good, long,
hard look at her, La Forge.

00:28:00.642 --> 00:28:05.875
See her for who she is,
not for what you want her to be.

00:28:11.419 --> 00:28:14.388
The life-form's patterns
are stable, Captain.

00:28:14.422 --> 00:28:17.391
It seems able to withstand
the solar radiation.

00:28:17.425 --> 00:28:19.416
Good. Ensign, set a course
for the Guernica system.

00:28:19.461 --> 00:28:20.428
Aye, sir.

00:28:20.462 --> 00:28:21.554
We're not staying?

00:28:21.596 --> 00:28:22.688
No, Number One.

00:28:22.731 --> 00:28:23.891
We've done all we can to help.

00:28:23.932 --> 00:28:24.921
Now it's time to move on.

00:28:24.966 --> 00:28:27.457
This creature can
continue its existence

00:28:27.502 --> 00:28:30.335
without any further
interference from us.

00:28:30.372 --> 00:28:32.602
It might be wise to put
some distance between us

00:28:32.641 --> 00:28:34.040
before we initiate warp drive.

00:28:34.075 --> 00:28:37.943
Very well. 500 kph, Ensign.

00:28:38.013 --> 00:28:39.742
Engage.

00:28:47.789 --> 00:28:50.485
Captain, it is following us.

00:28:50.525 --> 00:28:53.585
Maintaining a distance
of... four kilometers.

00:28:53.628 --> 00:28:54.856
Directly astern.

00:28:54.896 --> 00:28:57.126
17 degrees to port, Ensign.

00:28:57.165 --> 00:28:58.257
Aye, sir.

00:28:58.300 --> 00:29:00.291
It is turning with us, sir.

00:29:00.335 --> 00:29:02.599
Increase to half impulse.

00:29:04.706 --> 00:29:06.731
It is matching our velocity.

00:29:06.775 --> 00:29:10.370
It's imprinted on us.

00:29:10.412 --> 00:29:13.040
It thinks the Enterprise
is its mother.

00:29:15.650 --> 00:29:17.117
Change in energy reading, sir.

00:29:17.152 --> 00:29:19.848
I am reading an internal buildup
of gamma particles...

00:29:19.888 --> 00:29:21.378
Its velocity is increasing.

00:29:21.423 --> 00:29:23.391
It is moving directly
toward the ship.

00:29:23.425 --> 00:29:25.290
Evasive maneuvers. Full...

00:29:26.828 --> 00:29:28.125
Report.

00:29:28.163 --> 00:29:30.256
Minor damage.

00:29:30.298 --> 00:29:33.165
The creature is now in direct
contact with the hull, sir.

00:29:33.201 --> 00:29:34.828
On screen.

00:29:42.677 --> 00:29:44.110
Mr. Data?

00:29:44.145 --> 00:29:46.079
Sir, the life-form
is draining energy

00:29:46.114 --> 00:29:47.945
directly
from the fusion reactors.

00:29:47.983 --> 00:29:50.952
It's feeding off the
energy of the Enterprise

00:29:51.019 --> 00:29:52.850
as it would from its mother.

00:29:52.888 --> 00:29:55.652
What action should we take, sir?

00:29:57.659 --> 00:29:58.921
None, Lieutenant.

00:30:04.499 --> 00:30:06.467
None at all.

00:30:13.675 --> 00:30:16.143
Captain's Log, supplemental.

00:30:16.177 --> 00:30:18.941
Since the newborn
has attached itself to the hull

00:30:18.980 --> 00:30:21.346
it has been making
greater and greater demands

00:30:21.383 --> 00:30:23.647
on the ship's energy,
but we have been able

00:30:23.685 --> 00:30:25.915
to stabilize
our power systems temporarily.

00:30:25.954 --> 00:30:28.946
How long before the power drain
becomes critical, Mr. La Forge?

00:30:28.990 --> 00:30:30.514
If it continues to increase
at the same rate

00:30:30.558 --> 00:30:32.219
six, maybe seven hours.

00:30:32.260 --> 00:30:33.522
We may be able
to modify the engine

00:30:33.561 --> 00:30:34.994
to extend that
a little longer, Captain.

00:30:35.096 --> 00:30:36.757
Your help would be
appreciated, Doctor.

00:30:36.798 --> 00:30:38.891
By then, Junior may
not need us anymore.

00:30:38.934 --> 00:30:41.767
Mr. Data, is there any way
to determine

00:30:41.803 --> 00:30:44.271
what the destination
of the parent

00:30:44.306 --> 00:30:45.273
might have been?

00:30:45.307 --> 00:30:46.569
I can attempt to extrapolate

00:30:46.608 --> 00:30:49.202
from the heading it was on
when we encountered it, sir.

00:30:49.244 --> 00:30:50.541
Perhaps it was on its way

00:30:50.578 --> 00:30:53.741
to provide a safe and supportive
environment for its newborn.

00:30:53.782 --> 00:30:56.717
We might be able to deliver it
to the same destination.

00:30:56.751 --> 00:30:57.979
Which brings up the question

00:30:58.019 --> 00:31:00.180
of how do we get Junior off
the hull once we get there.

00:31:00.221 --> 00:31:03.952
It's almost completely covering
the door of Shuttle Bay Two.

00:31:03.992 --> 00:31:04.959
If we open the door

00:31:05.026 --> 00:31:07.426
and deactivate the atmospheric
force field...

00:31:07.462 --> 00:31:09.123
The pressure
from inside the ship

00:31:09.164 --> 00:31:10.825
might push it
away from the hull.

00:31:10.865 --> 00:31:13.561
Make it so.

00:31:13.601 --> 00:31:14.568
Sir?

00:31:14.602 --> 00:31:16.661
Is the appellation "Junior"

00:31:16.705 --> 00:31:19.435
to be the life-form's
official name?

00:31:19.474 --> 00:31:20.964
No, it is not.

00:31:24.879 --> 00:31:26.346
We can save a lot of energy

00:31:26.381 --> 00:31:28.372
just by improving
engine efficiency.

00:31:28.416 --> 00:31:29.974
We've run
into similar problems before.

00:31:30.085 --> 00:31:32.451
That's actually why I reoriented
the dilithium crystal.

00:31:32.487 --> 00:31:34.717
And why you added
the mid-range phase adjusters.

00:31:34.756 --> 00:31:35.780
Right.

00:31:35.824 --> 00:31:37.314
Commander, it seems
that you've made

00:31:37.359 --> 00:31:39.156
a lot more modifications
than I'm aware of.

00:31:39.194 --> 00:31:41.185
Do you have a file on
all the work you've done?

00:31:41.229 --> 00:31:42.423
Mm-hmm.
It's in the computer.

00:31:42.464 --> 00:31:43.431
Good.

00:31:43.465 --> 00:31:44.727
Picard to La Forge.

00:31:44.766 --> 00:31:45.790
La Forge here.

00:31:45.834 --> 00:31:47.995
Commander, I need to see you
on the Bridge.

00:31:48.036 --> 00:31:49.663
On my way, Captain.

00:31:49.704 --> 00:31:50.898
You go on ahead, Doctor.

00:31:50.939 --> 00:31:52.372
Ensign Pavlick
can show you the file

00:31:52.407 --> 00:31:53.533
on the engine modifications.

00:31:59.414 --> 00:32:03.214
"Phase coils upgraded
to 55 field densities.

00:32:03.251 --> 00:32:07.711
Plasma inducers interlinked
with generator."

00:32:07.756 --> 00:32:08.723
Ensign?

00:32:08.757 --> 00:32:10.657
Would there be any other files

00:32:10.692 --> 00:32:13.786
with data on the original
engine specifications?

00:32:13.828 --> 00:32:15.261
I believe so, Doctor.

00:32:19.534 --> 00:32:22.970
This file utilizes
the prototype engine schematic.

00:32:23.038 --> 00:32:24.972
It's a holographic program

00:32:25.006 --> 00:32:28.305
set in the drafting room
at Utopia Planitia.

00:32:28.343 --> 00:32:31.437
I'll run it on Holodeck Three.

00:32:39.287 --> 00:32:41.915
Computer, replay program 9140

00:32:41.956 --> 00:32:45.187
engine schematic
at Utopia Planitia.

00:32:45.226 --> 00:32:48.389
Program loaded and ready.

00:32:53.435 --> 00:32:55.164
She went where?

00:32:55.203 --> 00:32:56.329
Holodeck Three, sir.

00:32:56.371 --> 00:32:57.565
I didn't think

00:32:57.605 --> 00:32:59.505
there was anything wrong
with her seeing the file.

00:32:59.541 --> 00:33:00.735
No, of course not.

00:33:00.775 --> 00:33:02.640
Nothing at all!

00:33:02.677 --> 00:33:05.908
I'm with you every day, Geordi.

00:33:05.947 --> 00:33:07.812
Every time you look
at this engine

00:33:07.849 --> 00:33:09.043
you're looking at me.

00:33:09.084 --> 00:33:11.644
Every time you touch it,
it's me.

00:33:16.424 --> 00:33:17.857
Computer, freeze program.

00:33:19.227 --> 00:33:22.560
Now... I understand.

00:33:22.597 --> 00:33:24.292
No, you don't.

00:33:24.332 --> 00:33:26.129
It's not the way this may look.

00:33:26.167 --> 00:33:29.500
I called up a replay
of the program file.

00:33:29.537 --> 00:33:32.097
I was all ready to compliment
you again, Commander

00:33:32.140 --> 00:33:34.199
for constructing a program

00:33:34.242 --> 00:33:36.369
which contained
the prototype engine.

00:33:36.411 --> 00:33:38.106
So that you would always have

00:33:38.146 --> 00:33:40.740
a baseline reference
for your modifications.

00:33:40.782 --> 00:33:45.981
And now I find
that it's all about...

00:33:46.087 --> 00:33:47.076
a fantasy plaything.

00:33:47.122 --> 00:33:48.089
It's not like that.

00:33:48.123 --> 00:33:49.090
I swear...

00:33:49.124 --> 00:33:51.615
I'm outraged by this!

00:33:51.659 --> 00:33:53.957
I have been invaded, violated!

00:33:53.995 --> 00:33:56.327
How dare you use me like this?

00:33:56.364 --> 00:33:58.195
How far did it go anyway?

00:33:58.233 --> 00:33:59.632
Was it good for you?

00:33:59.667 --> 00:34:01.191
Nothing like that happened.

00:34:01.236 --> 00:34:03.261
It was a professional
collaboration.

00:34:03.304 --> 00:34:04.430
Oh, I can tell.

00:34:04.472 --> 00:34:05.939
"Every time you're touching
the engine

00:34:05.974 --> 00:34:06.941
you're touching me"?

00:34:06.975 --> 00:34:07.942
Real professional!

00:34:07.976 --> 00:34:09.534
Look, if you watched
the whole program

00:34:09.577 --> 00:34:10.737
you saw what it was.

00:34:10.778 --> 00:34:12.245
We were working together

00:34:12.280 --> 00:34:14.714
to solve a problem
in a crisis situation.

00:34:14.749 --> 00:34:16.580
How do I know how far it went?

00:34:16.618 --> 00:34:18.950
How many other programs
did you create?

00:34:19.020 --> 00:34:22.353
Perhaps dozens of them,
one for every day of the week.

00:34:22.390 --> 00:34:23.414
One for every mood!

00:34:23.458 --> 00:34:25.653
All right, look.

00:34:25.693 --> 00:34:28.594
Ever since you came on board,
you've been badgering me.

00:34:28.630 --> 00:34:29.597
And I've taken it.

00:34:29.631 --> 00:34:31.496
I've shown you courtesy

00:34:31.533 --> 00:34:34.297
and respect, and a hell
of a lot of patience.

00:34:34.335 --> 00:34:35.927
Oh, no, no, no, no.
Wait a minute.

00:34:35.970 --> 00:34:39.235
I've tried to understand you.

00:34:39.274 --> 00:34:40.969
I've tried
to get along with you.

00:34:41.042 --> 00:34:43.806
And in return you've accused,
tried and convicted me

00:34:43.845 --> 00:34:46.279
without even bothering
to hear my side of it?

00:34:46.314 --> 00:34:48.805
So, I'm guilty, okay?

00:34:48.850 --> 00:34:51.842
But not of what you think.

00:34:51.886 --> 00:34:54.286
Of something much worse.

00:34:54.322 --> 00:34:58.782
I'm guilty
of reaching out to you

00:34:58.826 --> 00:35:02.922
of hoping we could connect.

00:35:03.031 --> 00:35:08.594
I'm guilty
of a terrible crime, Doctor.

00:35:10.271 --> 00:35:12.569
I offered you friendship.

00:35:24.884 --> 00:35:28.581
Captain, its total volume
has increased by 8.5%

00:35:28.621 --> 00:35:30.088
in the last three hours.

00:35:30.122 --> 00:35:32.386
I now read it
at 46 million cubic meters.

00:35:32.425 --> 00:35:34.655
Captain, I have completed
the analysis

00:35:34.694 --> 00:35:36.889
of the parent's course
through the system.

00:35:36.929 --> 00:35:38.794
It was headed
for an asteroid belt.

00:35:39.999 --> 00:35:43.093
Ensign Rager,
set a course 259 mark 318.

00:35:43.135 --> 00:35:44.124
Half impulse.

00:35:44.170 --> 00:35:45.228
Aye, sir.

00:35:45.271 --> 00:35:48.468
Hold a position 500 kilometers
from the periphery

00:35:48.507 --> 00:35:49.974
of the asteroid field.

00:35:50.042 --> 00:35:51.031
Aye, sir.

00:35:58.117 --> 00:36:01.086
Difficulty getting
a clear sensor reading

00:36:01.120 --> 00:36:02.883
beyond 4,000 kilometers.

00:36:02.922 --> 00:36:06.085
The asteroids contain
large quantities of meklinite

00:36:06.125 --> 00:36:08.525
which is interfering
with our scanners.

00:36:08.561 --> 00:36:11.860
I am also detecting
traces of Kefnium

00:36:11.898 --> 00:36:15.356
a compound found in the outer
shell of the parent being.

00:36:15.401 --> 00:36:17.028
It is likely the asteroids

00:36:17.069 --> 00:36:19.867
provide sustenance
for this life-form, sir.

00:36:19.906 --> 00:36:21.203
We could leave the child here.

00:36:21.240 --> 00:36:23.606
If Data's right, it would have
an ample supply of food.

00:36:23.643 --> 00:36:24.610
Agreed.

00:36:24.644 --> 00:36:26.407
Mr. La Forge, are you ready

00:36:26.445 --> 00:36:28.743
to separate our guest
from the hull?

00:36:28.781 --> 00:36:29.748
Ready, Captain.

00:36:29.782 --> 00:36:30.771
Proceed.

00:36:41.527 --> 00:36:45.759
I am deactivating
the atmospheric force field now.

00:36:55.975 --> 00:36:57.135
Engineering, report.

00:36:57.176 --> 00:36:59.974
The power drain
just jumped to 93%, sir.

00:37:00.012 --> 00:37:02.207
Captain,
the offspring is emitting

00:37:02.248 --> 00:37:03.772
high-frequency
radio transmissions.

00:37:03.816 --> 00:37:05.113
Is it trying to communicate?

00:37:05.151 --> 00:37:06.914
The power drain is increasing.

00:37:06.986 --> 00:37:09.147
Approaching auto-shutdown.

00:37:09.188 --> 00:37:10.587
Take the engines off-line.

00:37:10.623 --> 00:37:12.614
Supplement
with auxiliary power only.

00:37:12.658 --> 00:37:14.683
All decks go
to emergency level seven.

00:37:14.727 --> 00:37:16.922
Life-support
and critical operations only.

00:37:17.029 --> 00:37:18.860
Mr. La Forge,
what is your status?

00:37:18.898 --> 00:37:19.922
Sorry, Captain.

00:37:19.966 --> 00:37:22.833
The bay has been
completely depressurized

00:37:22.868 --> 00:37:24.927
but... it's still hanging on.

00:37:25.004 --> 00:37:27.837
I am detecting other radio
transmissions, Captain.

00:37:27.873 --> 00:37:31.866
Sensors detect movement
within the asteroid field.

00:37:31.911 --> 00:37:34.539
Bearing 257 mark 161.

00:37:34.580 --> 00:37:36.673
On screen.

00:37:37.750 --> 00:37:38.876
Magnify.

00:37:41.320 --> 00:37:43.618
At their current speed, sir

00:37:43.656 --> 00:37:48.593
the entities will intercept us
in... ten minutes, 31 seconds.

00:37:48.627 --> 00:37:49.924
Weapon status?

00:37:49.962 --> 00:37:51.327
Auxiliary power only.

00:37:51.364 --> 00:37:53.559
Two seconds'
phaser fire available.

00:38:16.288 --> 00:38:18.756
Ensign, power readings.

00:38:18.791 --> 00:38:20.759
We're on auxiliary generators.

00:38:20.793 --> 00:38:22.727
Life-support is functioning.

00:38:22.762 --> 00:38:23.820
That's about all.

00:38:23.863 --> 00:38:25.455
Keep your eye on that
generator console.

00:38:25.498 --> 00:38:28.194
We've got less than six minutes
to get that baby off our back

00:38:28.234 --> 00:38:29.565
before his relatives get here.

00:38:29.602 --> 00:38:33.538
Whatever we try, Junior responds
by sucking up more energy.

00:38:34.473 --> 00:38:35.599
Commander

00:38:35.641 --> 00:38:36.938
I have a thought...

00:38:37.043 --> 00:38:39.637
if you're interested.

00:38:39.678 --> 00:38:40.667
Of course.

00:38:40.713 --> 00:38:41.941
What is it?

00:38:42.014 --> 00:38:45.347
If the baby is nursing,
perhaps what we need

00:38:45.384 --> 00:38:47.944
is to find a way
to sour the milk.

00:38:48.020 --> 00:38:51.581
If we could contaminate
the energy he's feeding on

00:38:51.624 --> 00:38:52.955
we could try to...

00:38:52.992 --> 00:38:54.653
Make it unpalatable somehow.

00:38:54.693 --> 00:38:55.819
Uh-huh.

00:38:55.861 --> 00:38:58.887
But the emergency generators
are all we've got.

00:38:58.931 --> 00:39:02.162
And how do we modify them
without losing life-support?

00:39:02.201 --> 00:39:03.600
Exactly.

00:39:07.273 --> 00:39:08.604
Unless...

00:39:10.843 --> 00:39:11.901
What?

00:39:11.944 --> 00:39:13.036
Well...

00:39:13.079 --> 00:39:15.240
this is a space baby, right?

00:39:15.281 --> 00:39:17.875
I mean these creatures are born

00:39:17.917 --> 00:39:21.114
they live and die
in interstellar space.

00:39:21.153 --> 00:39:22.245
Apparently.

00:39:22.288 --> 00:39:23.915
Okay.

00:39:23.989 --> 00:39:28.289
All matter in space vibrates
in a specific radiation band.

00:39:28.327 --> 00:39:31.455
21 centimeters.

00:39:31.497 --> 00:39:33.556
Oh...

00:39:33.599 --> 00:39:36.466
Oh, that's good, Commander.

00:39:36.502 --> 00:39:38.163
That's very good.

00:39:38.204 --> 00:39:40.104
If we could alter
the power frequency

00:39:40.139 --> 00:39:41.766
so that it's completely foreign

00:39:41.807 --> 00:39:43.900
to the life-form's
natural vibrations...

00:39:43.943 --> 00:39:45.342
Might just give us enough

00:39:45.377 --> 00:39:47.641
to pour a little vinegar
in baby's milk.

00:39:47.680 --> 00:39:49.341
Yeah, we have to be careful
though.

00:39:49.381 --> 00:39:52.350
If we upset it this time, we
might lose auxiliary power, too.

00:39:52.384 --> 00:39:55.251
If we're gradual enough,
it won't be such a shock.

00:39:55.287 --> 00:39:57.380
Hopefully, it'll just
lose interest.

00:39:59.325 --> 00:40:01.088
La Forge to Bridge.

00:40:01.127 --> 00:40:02.594
Go ahead.

00:40:02.628 --> 00:40:06.120
Captain, Dr. Brahms and I
have a plan.

00:40:19.678 --> 00:40:22.806
Two minutes until the creatures
intercept, Captain.

00:40:31.257 --> 00:40:34.749
Captain, we're ready down here.

00:40:34.793 --> 00:40:36.317
Proceed.

00:40:36.362 --> 00:40:39.388
Lowering wavelength
in the energy system...

00:40:39.431 --> 00:40:40.398
now.

00:40:40.432 --> 00:40:42.764
Reading 18...

00:40:42.801 --> 00:40:44.666
fifteen...

00:40:44.703 --> 00:40:46.500
thirteen...

00:40:46.539 --> 00:40:48.439
eleven...

00:40:48.474 --> 00:40:50.101
eight...

00:40:50.142 --> 00:40:51.769
five...

00:40:51.810 --> 00:40:53.539
three.

00:40:53.579 --> 00:40:55.706
Now at the two-centimeter level.

00:40:55.748 --> 00:40:57.875
Any reaction, Bridge?

00:40:57.917 --> 00:40:59.009
Negative.

00:40:59.084 --> 00:41:01.450
I detect no reduction
in the life-form's

00:41:01.487 --> 00:41:02.613
rate of energy consumption.

00:41:02.655 --> 00:41:05.419
One minute, 30 seconds
to intercept.

00:41:05.457 --> 00:41:07.322
Not sour enough.

00:41:08.627 --> 00:41:11.960
Leah, take it down further.

00:41:12.031 --> 00:41:14.625
Reading one...

00:41:14.667 --> 00:41:16.430
point eight...

00:41:16.468 --> 00:41:18.299
point four...

00:41:18.337 --> 00:41:19.998
point two.

00:41:24.843 --> 00:41:27.539
I guess it noticed
what we're doing.

00:41:27.580 --> 00:41:30.606
The life-form is emitting
its high-frequency transmission.

00:41:30.649 --> 00:41:32.310
Energy consumption is rising.

00:41:32.351 --> 00:41:36.811
Captain, the creatures are
accelerating their approach.

00:41:36.855 --> 00:41:38.152
They are changing color.

00:41:38.190 --> 00:41:39.589
Mr. La Forge!

00:41:39.625 --> 00:41:41.820
Captain,
just a little more time.

00:41:41.860 --> 00:41:43.259
Leah, nudge it down
even further.

00:41:43.295 --> 00:41:44.819
Toward.02.

00:41:46.398 --> 00:41:48.525
30 seconds to intercept.

00:41:48.567 --> 00:41:50.558
Point oh eight...

00:41:50.603 --> 00:41:52.537
oh five...

00:41:52.571 --> 00:41:54.402
oh three.

00:41:54.440 --> 00:41:56.670
Now at.02 centimeters.

00:41:56.709 --> 00:41:59.542
Auxiliary generators
losing power, Captain.

00:42:12.658 --> 00:42:14.956
The entity has disengaged, sir.

00:42:15.060 --> 00:42:18.257
Power levels are returning
to normal, Captain.

00:42:24.303 --> 00:42:26.567
Bring the engines on-line
and take us out of here.

00:42:26.605 --> 00:42:28.197
Aye, sir.

00:42:28.240 --> 00:42:33.007
Mr. La Forge, Dr. Brahms,
congratulations.

00:42:35.014 --> 00:42:36.914
You've weaned the baby.

00:42:39.518 --> 00:42:41.509
Good work.

00:42:41.553 --> 00:42:43.384
You, too.
